From 37719dabeef1a0d03a0faf86d6812f1beea8244a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marouene Boubakri <marouene.boubakri@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 02:02:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] IIOTSOL1-1586: IsoMux: support multiple TLS cert chains for
 ISO 15118-2 +  ISO 15118-20 simultaneously

IsoMux's TLS server loads exactly one cert chain into its SSL_CTX
via the single `security` requirement on its module manifest. That
one chain must satisfy whichever protocol profile the EV negotiates.
There is no single cert that satisfies both:

  * ISO 15118-2 Annex H: SECC leaf must be NIST P-256 with
    ecdsa-with-SHA256 signature.
  * ISO 15118-20 Annex F: SECC leaf must be NIST P-521 with
    ecdsa-with-SHA512 signature.

Deployments serving both protocols simultaneously - e.g. ISO 15118-2
PnC (which requires TLS) alongside ISO 15118-20 EIM (which also
requires TLS, with a different cert profile) - cannot work today.
With a P-256 leaf wired into IsoMux, ISO 15118-20 EVs reject the
cert during CertificateVerify (alert 51, decrypt_error); with a
P-521 leaf wired in, ISO 15118-2 EVs do the same.

OpenSSL natively supports multiple cert chains in one SSL_CTX and
selects at ClientHello time based on the client's
signature_algorithms extension (RFC 8446 section 4.2.3). The
underlying tls::Server type already exposes `config.chains` as a
vector. Only the IsoMux glue layer was assuming one cert.

Add an optional second EvseSecurity requirement, `security_secondary`,
on IsoMux. When wired, both EvseSecurity instances are queried for
V2G leaf certs at TLS server build time, and both chains are added
to `config.chains`. OpenSSL then handles per-handshake cert selection
based on what the client EV advertises.

Backward-compatible: existing configs that wire only `security` keep
working unchanged. Only configs that explicitly wire `security_secondary`
get the multi-chain behavior. The patch does not change the existing
single-chain code path.

Recommended wiring for a deployment serving both ISO 15118-2 PnC and
ISO 15118-20 EIM:

  EvseSecurity_iso2:    # iso2/ cert tree (P-256/SHA-256)
    module: EvseSecurity
    config_module:
      ...

  EvseSecurity_iso20:   # iso20/ cert tree (P-521/SHA-512)
    module: EvseSecurity
    config_module:
      ...

  IsoMux0:
    module: IsoMux
    connections:
      security:
        - module_id: EvseSecurity_iso20  # or _iso2; the order does
          implementation_id: main         # not matter
      security_secondary:
        - module_id: EvseSecurity_iso2   # whichever wasn't in security
          implementation_id: main

Note: this patch does not require companion patches to the
LeafCertificateType enum or EvseSecurity API. Each EvseSecurity
instance keeps its existing single-cert-per-V2G-query semantics.
The multi-chain handling is entirely on IsoMux's side, wiring two
existing-API EvseSecurity instances.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Marouene Boubakri <maroueneboubakri@nxp.com>
